{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And all its spoil you shall gather.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'and not the spoil of Heaven' — meaning that the spoil of Heaven escaped. From this they said: consecrated objects within it are redeemed, that is, they are not burned, but are like other consecrated property that requires redemption, because it is 'spoil of Heaven.' And likewise included in this is Second Tithe within it, which is not burned, even though it is eaten by an Israelite, because it is called 'consecrated' and they fall under the category of consecrated property. And likewise consecrated scrolls within it — we do not say they are burned; rather, whether Second Tithe, consecrated scrolls, or anything that is consecrated, they are not subject to burning but require burial (genizah)." "<b>A whole-offering to HaShem your Elohim.</b> It is entirely for the Holy One, blessed be He; you have no permission to derive benefit from it, but rather you must burn it for His glory, may He be exalted. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: R. Shimon said — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: If you execute justice upon the wayward city, I account it for you as though you had offered before Me a burnt-offering, which is 'a whole-offering to HaShem,' as it is said (Exodus 32:29): ״מלאו ידכם היום לה' כי איש בבנו ובאחיו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:13.509054961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}